 "asked_at": "2026-10-18T00:45+08:00",
 "answer": "Whether you should wear a mask outside in Singapore depends on your health status, how long you plan to be outdoors, and the current air quality (due to the regional haze). \n\nAccording to guidelines from the Ministry of Health (MOH) and the National Environment Agency (NEA):\n\n### 1. If you are a healthy individual:\n* **Short commutes or indoor activities:** You generally **do not need** to wear an N95 mask (or equivalents like KN95, KF94, or FFP2) when commuting to work, school, or staying indoors. \n* **Extended outdoor activities:** If you need to spend *several hours* outdoors when local PM2.5 levels or PSI readings are in the very high or unhealthy ranges, you may consider wearing a well-fitted N95 mask or equivalent to reduce exposure. Otherwise, the primary advice is to minimize prolonged or strenuous outdoor physical exertion.\n\n### 2. If you are in a vulnerable group (Elderly, pregnant women, children, or those with chronic heart/lung conditions):\n* **Vulnerable individuals** (such as pregnant women, young children, or those with asthma or chronic heart/lung diseases) are advised to **avoid or minimize outdoor activities** when air quality reaches unhealthy-to-very-unhealthy levels.\n* If you must be outdoors for an extended period during high or very high PM2.5 levels, you should consider wearing a mask. \n* *Note:* Anyone (especially those with severe pre-existing heart or lung problems) who experiences breathing difficulties at rest or while wearing a mask should consult a doctor before using an N95 mask.\n\n### What to check right now:\nBecause conditions can fluctuate, check the real-time 1-hour PM2.5 concentrations and the 24-hr PSI on the **[myENV app](https://www.nea.gov.sg/)** or **[haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg)** before heading out:\n* **Normal / Elevated PM2.5:** Masks are generally not necessary for short exposure.\n* **High / Very High PM2.5:** Recommended if you are vulnerable or forced to stay outdoors for an extended time.",
